/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-workspace-SuperGrok1-5/122b3aee-fa74-43c0-936d-39ff1eca854f/subagents/workflows/wf_42c6c6ad-b9e/agent-add6cd61c010cc195.jsonl:1144:{"parentUuid":"143220ba-dffa-4927-89ef-592977680557","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"ad6abc3e-c73d-410d-b091-6f5fde53815e","agentId":"add6cd61c010cc195","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Single-shot subagent task (spawned by orchestration script — final text response is returned verbatim as the return value, must be concise, no \"Done\" confirmations, report findings directly not in files): \"In /workspace/SuperGrok1.5: maximize L3-TC megakernel cells for model=mamba, one cell finished at a time, each maxed BEFORE moving on. First (mamba lane only): profile + FIX the TC-vs-scalar 0.46x bottleneck (per-sample scan serialization; multi-CTA tiling). Per cell: optimize until roofline-verified flat (warp-occupancy, tile shapes, dW ownership; eager/scalar are test refs only); gates = tests/hw/test_l3tc_tail_gate.py + wiring_check.py per cell (no suppression; blocked cells loud + cited); measure quiet (CUDA_MPS_PIPE_DIRECTORY=/nonexistent), B=16384. Order opts: lion,adamw,grokfast first (cheap), then grokadamw(3 mechanisms), prodigy/muon/SG11/SG15/looksam/neuralgrok/SG2 per their INTEGRATION specs. EDIT ONLY mamba stage/launcher files + shared opt_components via single-writer rule: lane edits opt headers ONLY for mamba-needed tails, append-only. No commit. Report per-cell TF/s + frac.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - L3-TC persistent megakernel: ONE CUDA kernel per training step runs real model fwd+bwd + optimizer math, separated by in-kernel grid barriers (no CUDA graphs, no intermediate launches)\n   - Mamba selective-SSM: in_proj/x_proj/dt_proj/out_proj projections (the 4 TC-accelerated wgmma GEMMs) + scalar selective-scan recurrence + conv1d (non-causal k=3) + LayerNorm. d=128, d_inner=256, state=16, dt_rank=8, kSeq=8, 28 param tensors / 259425 elems, kPHead=97, kVocab=99\n   - Persistent kernel design: gridDim=#SMs (132 on H100), one-CTA-per-SM, 256 threads/CTA, hand-built sense-reversing GridBarrier (megakernel_common.cuh §1.4, two-fence visibility model assuming 1 CTA/SM)\n   - Phase structure: P0 zero partials → B0 → P1 tile-parallel fwd+bwd → B1 → P2 (dW GEMM + bias + cross-CTA reduce + embed owner-scan) → B2 → P3 optimizer tail\n   - Profiling: clock64() phase brackets (max-CTA reconciliation = wall, since grid barrier waits for straggler); cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMultiprocessor; SG_MBTC_BYPASS_* differential profiling\n   - Register-pinned occupancy: 255 reg/thread → occ=1; __launch_bounds__(256,2) caps to 128 reg → occ=2\n   - Roofline: bf16_tc peak 989.4e12, fp32_cuda 66.9e12, hbm_bw 3.35e12; achieved=FLOPs_per_step/wall; FLOPs are GEMM-counted (path-independent)\n   - Determinism: fixed CTA/thread ownership + ascending-c reduce order = bit-identical fp32 sums regardless of which thread computes\n   - Single-writer rule: each agent owns specific files; sibling agents concurrently edit decoder/vit files\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh (MODIFIED — my edits)\n     - Contains mbtc_forward_tile, mbtc_backward_tile, mbtc_partial_reduce, mbtc_dw_biases, mbtc_dw_run_tile\n     - FIX 1: rewrote mbtc_partial_reduce from by-tensor (only kNumPartTensors=16 of 132 CTAs work) to flat-element striping across all 132 CTAs. Added mbtc_part_flat_map (register-only segment cursor, NO __shared__ which caused smem overflow):\n       ```\n       __device__ __forceinline__ void mbtc_part_flat_map(int64_t e, int& seg, int64_t& gdst) {\n           int gidx, numel; int64_t poff;\n           mbtc_part_slot(seg, gidx, poff, numel);\n           if (e < poff) { seg = 0; mbtc_part_slot(seg, gidx, poff, numel); }\n           while (e >= poff + numel) { ++seg; mbtc_part_slot(seg, gidx, poff, numel); }\n           gdst = kMambaOffsets[gidx] + (e - poff);\n       }\n       ```\n       Then mbtc_partial_reduce strides e over (cta*blockDim+tid, stride=nCTA*blockDim), sums ascending-c, writes grad[gdst].\n     - FIX 2: rewrote mbtc_dw_biases to add (int cta, int nCTA) params and single-owner striping over flattened bias-output space (was: every CTA recomputed full O(T) sum + race-wrote same grad slot = 18.9% uniform cost). New signature: `mbtc_dw_biases(const MbDwSpec spec[8], float* grad, int cta, int nCTA)`\n     - NOTE: this file ALSO contains pre-existing pipelining/split-K infra (SG_TUNED_MB_GEMM_STAGES default 2, kMbDwSplitK default 4, stage_k/issue_k, mb_dw_part_floats) that is NOT mine (sibling/prior-session), active in all measurements, gate-valid\n     - kNumPartTensors = kLayers*6+4 = 16; kPartElems = 24033; OptId enum: AdamW=0, Lion=1, Grokfast=2, GrokAdamW=3, LookSAM=4\n\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh (MODIFIED — my edits)\n     - Added SG_MB_TC_PROFILE macro (default 0, inert in production) + clock64 phase brackets in fused_mamba_megakernel_tc\n     - Added SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM (DEFAULT 1 after revert) + SG_MBTC_LAUNCH_BOUNDS macro:\n       ```\n       #ifndef SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM\n       #define SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM 1\n       #endif\n       #if SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM >= 1\n       #define SG_MBTC_LAUNCH_BOUNDS __launch_bounds__(SG_MB_TC_MEGA_BLOCK, SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM)\n       ```\n       Kernel uses `__global__ void SG_MBTC_LAUNCH_BOUNDS fused_mamba_megakernel_tc(...)`. Comment documents occ=2 measured 1.14x faster but DETERMINISM-UNSAFE (A/A/A max|Δ|=2.3e-10 vs occ=1 bit-identical; barrier substrate fix in megakernel_common.cuh out of lane)\n     - Added mb_tc_launched_nctas<Opt>(dev, ncta_cap) host helper returning occ*n_sms (waves logic) so callers size workspace correctly\n     - Launcher: `unsigned waves = (SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM >= 2 && occ > 1) ? (unsigned)occ : 1u; unsigned launch_ctas = (unsigned)n_sms * waves;`\n     - dw_biases call updated: `mbtc::mbtc_dw_biases(spec, grad, cta, nCTA);`\n\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc.cu (MODIFIED — my edit)\n     - tc_effective_nctas now uses mb_tc_launched_nctas<OptId::AdamW>(dev, ncta_cap) for correct workspace sizing (falls back to n_sms if occ query fails). Exposes tc_train_step, scalar_train_step, TOTAL=259425\n\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_mamba_real_adamw_tc_launcher.cu (MODIFIED — my edit)\n     - The WIRED launcher TU (globbed into _ops, dispatches AdamW/Lion/Grokfast). nCTA sizing now uses mb_tc_launched_nctas<OptId::AdamW>\n\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba3.cuh (READ ONLY — DO NOT MODIFY)\n     - Contains mb_scan_fwd, mb_scan_bwd, mb_conv1d_fwd, mb_layernorm_fwd. The scan keeps h[16]/A[16]/hh[]/gh[]/dt_save in registers (seq=8 exploit). Bmat[t][s]/Cmat[t][s] read by all 256 channel-threads (broadcast, already L1-cached). This is the scalar recurrence floor.\n\n   - /workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/opt_components.cuh (READ ONLY — NOT edited, no mamba tail needed)\n     - FusedOptState fields: exp_avg, exp_avg_sq, ema, alpha (grokfast strength), lamb (grokfast amplification). apply_optimizer<OptId::Grokfast> cold-starts ema=grad at step==1, then grokfast_fused_step: e_new=alpha*ema+(1-alpha)*g, g_amp=g+lamb*e_new, m/v adam-style\n\n   - /tmp scratch files (NOT in repo): build_mamba_tc.py, run_prof.py, mamba_prof_tu.cu, diff_phases.py, occ_cmp.py, time_tc.py, tail_gate_mamba.cu, run_tailgate.py, gf_gate.py, smoke_tg.py\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Profiler double* misalignment (\"misaligned address\"): fixed by rounding prof float offset up to even (8-byte aligned) in both kernel and host\n   - __shared__ MbPartSegTable smem overflow (compute-sanitizer: invalid __shared__ write in forward stage_kmajor_tile, addr past MbTcSmem): function-local __shared__ collided with kernel's MbTcSmem staging arena. Fixed by eliminating __shared__, using register-only segment cursor in mbtc_part_flat_map\n   - test_tc_proj_dw_exact rel=1.0 transient FAIL: was a stale .so from mid-edit; clean rebuild → 5/5 pass\n   - occ=2 determinism FAIL (mandated gate (2): losses not bit-identical): discriminator proved occ=2 breaks grid-barrier determinism. REVERTED default to occ=1. (Advisor: \"occ=2 co-residency breaks determinism — the barrier is one-CTA-per-SM by design; fix is in megakernel_common.cuh = out of lane\")\n   - Wrong OptId enum values (lion=8/grokfast=4 = LookSAM): launches hit default→cudaErrorInvalidValue. Fixed to AdamW=0,Lion=1,Grokfast=2\n   - _ops build FAILED repeatedly: sibling's decoder bug (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:459 \"total undefined\" + bindings.cpp pybind mismatch, task #44). NOT my files (single-writer). Eventually sibling fixed it; 01:13 build succeeded\n   - Stale JIT lock files (tail_gate_mamba/lock 0 bytes from killed builds) caused load() to hang on file_baton. Fixed with `find /root/.cache/torch_extensions -name lock -delete`\n   - Self-inflicted: my `pkill -f \"[r]un_tailgate\"` killed BOTH background AND foreground gate runs (same script name), making me think they hung when I killed them\n   - Noisy 289ms/133ms measurements: GPU clock-ramp artifacts (345MHz idle) + concurrent-build contention. Fixed with longer warmup (ramp to 1980MHz) + min-of-reps + measuring when no concurrent build\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   SOLVED: Root-caused the mamba TC bottleneck as occ=1 latency exposure + two grad-assembly bugs (partial_reduce 16/132 CTA participation, dw_biases 132x-redundant O(T) recompute). Landed 2 deterministic fixes (139.9→113.2ms ~19% from dw_biases alone, in-harness measured). Explored occ=2 (1.14x faster) but reverted for determinism (gate-mandated). Confirmed scan recurrence (~27-37% of wall) is the floor — it's in DO-NOT-MODIFY model_stage_mamba3.cuh and the projection GEMMs are essentially free (0.1% of wall by bypass diff = TC working perfectly). Final: 114.6ms, 1.718 TF/s, 0.702% bf16-roofline, deterministic, TC wins 2.17x vs scalar. All 3 cells (adamw/lion/grokfast) gate-green via real dispatch.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"In /workspace/SuperGrok1.5: maximize L3-TC megakernel cells for model=mamba, one cell finished at a time, each maxed BEFORE moving on. First (mamba lane only): profile + FIX the TC-vs-scalar 0.46x bottleneck (per-sample scan serialization; multi-CTA tiling). Per cell: optimize until roofline-verified flat (warp-occupancy, tile shapes, dW ownership; eager/scalar are test refs only); gates = tests/hw/test_l3tc_tail_gate.py + wiring_check.py per cell (no suppression; blocked cells loud + cited); measure quiet (CUDA_MPS_PIPE_DIRECTORY=/nonexistent), B=16384. Order opts: lion,adamw,grokfast first (cheap), then grokadamw(3 mechanisms), prodigy/muon/SG11/SG15/looksam/neuralgrok/SG2 per their INTEGRATION specs. EDIT ONLY mamba stage/launcher files + shared opt_components via single-writer rule: lane edits opt headers ONLY for mamba-needed tails, append-only. No commit. Report per-cell TF/s + frac.\"\n   - System reminder (memory/CLAUDE.md): \"No functionality suppression — fix components, never disable them\"; \"H100 MPS max parallelism — owner wants hardware saturation: MPS daemon + 14-worker fleet; quit kills daemon; pkill self-match gotcha\"; \"Portable megakernel components — all 33 cells from header-only portable components; contract at csrc/fused/COMPONENT_CONTRACT.md; no CUDA graphs\"; \"H100 durable requirements — PTX-maximal kernels, AdamW-grade callability, hw max-parallelism, roofline metric, no CUDA graphs, no suppression\"\n   - Final system message (for THIS summary): \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - The 