/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/subagents/agent-aecd237c42ad37eea.jsonl:331:{"parentUuid":"aac3d2db-225a-4218-9787-e0118c0da1f3","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"1a4547f5-851c-42c1-b3cc-befef46b14ad","agentId":"aecd237c42ad37eea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TZCrZxpsH4jVpZwjCt6UoJ","type":"tool_result","content":"284\tdef test_tc_single_step_grad_parity():\n285\t    \"\"\"(1) KEYSTONE: TC reduced grad vs the bf16-FAITHFUL fp64 oracle (rounds at\n286\t    the kernel's storage points). Loss rel ≤ 5e-3. The calibration witness\n287\t    (printed): kernel-vs-bf16faithful against bf16faithful-vs-fp64 (the floor)\n288\t    + the layer-0/layer-1 split (a real bug → early layers ≫ late).\"\"\"\n289\t    from tests.hw.mamba_oracle import mamba_param_layout\n290\t    mod = _build_tc_module()\n291\t    _disable_tf32()\n292\t    dev = \"cuda\"\n293\t    named = _eager_mamba_named(seed=123)\n294\t    B = 128\n295\t    g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(5)\n296\t    from tests.hw.mamba_oracle import VOCAB, P_HEAD, SEQ\n297\t    tokens = torch.randint(0, VOCAB, (B, SEQ), generator=g)\n298\t    targets = torch.randint(0, P_HEAD, (B,), generator=g)\n299\t    loss_o, grads_o = _bf16_faithful_mamba_oracle(named, tokens, targets)\n300\t    loss_fp, grads_fp = _pure_fp64_oracle(named, tokens, targets)\n301\t    params = _flat(named).to(dev)\n302\t    total = int(mod.TOTAL)\n303\t    state = torch.zeros(3 * total, dtype=torch.float32, device=dev)\n304\t    loss_k, kgrad = _run_tc_step(mod, params.clone(), tokens.to(dev), targets.to(dev),\n305\t                                 state, lr=1e-3, betas=(0.9, 0.98), wd=0.0, eps=1e-8, step=1)\n306\t    loss_k = float(loss_k.item()); kgrad = kgrad.cpu().double()\n307\t    rel_loss = abs(loss_k - loss_o) / (abs(loss_o) + 1e-30)\n308\t    print(f\"[mbtc] loss kernel={loss_k:.6f} bf16-oracle={loss_o:.6f} rel={rel_loss:.2e}\")\n309\t    assert rel_loss < _TC_LOSS_REL, f\"TC loss rel {rel_loss:.2e} > {_TC_LOSS_REL}\"\n310\t    lay = mamba_param_layout()\n311\t    worst = 0.0; worst_name = \"\"\n312\t    l0w, l1w, floor = [], [], 0.0\n313\t    PROJ = (\"in_proj.weight\", \"x_proj.weight\", \"dt_proj.weight\", \"out_proj.weight\")\n314\t    for name, off, sz, shape in zip(lay[\"names\"], lay[\"offsets\"], lay[\"sizes\"], lay[\"shapes\"]):\n315\t        kg = kgrad[off:off + sz].reshape(shape)\n316\t        og = grads_o[name]; fp = grads_fp[name].double()\n317\t        a = (kg - og).abs().max().item(); denom = og.abs().max().item() + 1e-30\n318\t        rel = a / denom\n319\t        bff = (og - fp).abs().max().item() / denom\n320\t        floor = max(floor, bff)\n321\t        is_proj_w = any(name.endswith(p) for p in PROJ)\n322\t        tol = _TC_GRAD_REL\n323\t        if \"layers.0\" in name and is_proj_w: l0w.append(rel)\n324\t        if \"layers.1\" in name and is_proj_w: l1w.append(rel)\n325\t        over = rel / tol\n326\t        if over > worst:\n327\t            worst = over; worst_name = f\"{name} (rel {rel:.2e} tol {tol})\"\n328\t        print(f\"  grad {name:28s} k-vs-bf16 {rel:.3e}  bf16-vs-fp64 {bff:.3e}  tol {tol}\")\n329\t    import statistics as st\n330\t    l0 = st.mean(l0w) if l0w else 0.0; l1 = st.mean(l1w) if l1w else 0.0\n331\t    print(f\"[mbtc] STRUCTURAL: layer0 proj-weight mean rel={l0:.3e}  layer1={l1:.3e}  \"\n332\t          f\"(real bug → layer0 ≫ layer1; bf16 noise → comparable)\")\n333\t    print(f\"[mbtc] bf16-floor (bf16faithful vs fp64) max over all grads = {floor:.3e}\")\n334\t    assert worst <= 1.0, f\"worst grad over tol: {worst_name} (over={worst:.2f}×)\"\n335\t\n336\t\n337\t@_GATE\n338\tdef test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands():"}]},"uuid":"6e0b1bdf-6d20-474c-b777-da1210d4fd49","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:20:21.934Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aac3d2db-225a-4218-9787-e0118c0da1f3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspace/SuperGrok1.5","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","version":"2.1.173","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"sprightly-pondering-dewdrop"}
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/subagents/agent-aecd237c42ad37eea.jsonl:332:{"parentUuid":"6e0b1bdf-6d20-474c-b777-da1210d4fd49","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aecd237c42ad37eea","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JgWQzeKnoJ7u3kGLouU3QZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I understand the test. It runs at **B=128** (not production scale). The `worst` is max(rel/tol). x_proj.weight layer0 has rel=115.7, tol=0.08 → over = 1446×. That's the trigger. \n\nThe fact that x_proj (Nout=40, 1 atom) is catastrophically wrong (115) while the structural diagnostic shows \"layer0 ≫ layer1\" points to a **real dW bug in the x_proj (odd, 1-atom) path**. But wait — in_proj (8 atoms) shows rel=1.025 which is also >tol=0.08. So multiple weights are affected.\n\nCritical realization: **B=128 → T = B·kSeq = 128·8 = 1024 → T/16 = 64**. The split-K G=4 → kc_steps = 64/4 = 16. That's fine (G | T/16). So split-K is active even at B=128.\n\nLet me think harder about x_proj. x_proj: Nout=40 (1 atom), Kin=dInner=256. N-tiling: Kin=256, N=128 → 2 N-tiles. So x_proj has 1 group × 2 N-tiles = 2 work items. The slot for each is `kMbDwIL*64*N = 2*64*128` floats. The engine runs MaxAtomsM=2, g_atoms=1, mbase=0. It issues 1 atom (40 valid rows). Writes lr∈[0,64) but only m<40 valid (srcA returns 0 for m≥40). The `out` writes `lr = m-mbase = m-0 = m`, for m∈[0,64) but only m<40 are real (the engine's epilogue emits rows 0..63 of the m64 atom; rows 40..63 get garbage from the padded srcA which returns 0 → so v=0 for those, harmless). Wait, actually the engine emits ALL 64 rows of the atom (frag_decode covers the full m64), and `out` is called for each with the computed v. For m≥40, srcA returned 0 so the accumulated v should be ~0. The `out` guard in splitk is `lr < kMbDwIL*64 = 128` → writes lr=0..63. Then reduce reads Nrow = min(40-0, 128) = 40 rows. So only rows 0..39 are scattered to grad. That seems correct.\n\nHmm, so why is x_proj wrong? Let me reconsider — maybe the bug is NOT x_proj-specific but a general dW issue, and x_proj just shows it most starkly. Let me reconsider the **reduce** `base` indexing. `base = gt * G * kMbDwTileFloats`. The slot in run_tile_splitk is `(gt*G + kc) * kMbDwTileFloats`. The reduce reads `base + kc*kMbDwTileFloats + row*N + col` = `gt*G*kMbDwTileFloats + kc*kMbDwTileFloats + row*N + col` = `(gt*G + kc)*kMbDwTileFloats + row*N + col`. Consistent. \n\nWait — `row*N` in the reduce, but the slot was written as `lr*N + n`. So slot layout is `[lr][n]` with stride N. Reduce reads `row*N + col`. Consistent. \n\nLet me look very carefully at the **mamba engine epilogue / issue**. Actually — let me reconsider the `kMbAtomsPerSlot` vs `kIL` discrepancy more carefully for the **dW** path specifically. In dW splitk, the engine is called with `MaxAtomsM = kMbDwIL = 2`. Inside the engine, `kIL = min(MaxAtomsM=2, kMbMaxIL=2) = 2`. And `kMbAtomsPerSlot = min(kAtomsM=2, kMbMaxIL=2) = 2`. So slot stride uses `s * kMbAtomsPerSlot + ai = s*2 + ai`. Allocation `S * kMbAtomsPerSlot = 2*2 = 4` tiles. Indices: s∈{0,1}, ai∈{0,1} → max `1*2+1 = 3` < 4. OK, in bounds.\n\nHmm, that's all correct. Let me actually empirically localize: is fwd correct (loss passes)? The test asserts `rel_loss < 5e-3` BEFORE the grad check. Since it failed on the GRAD assertion (line 334), the LOSS check passed → **fwd is correct**. So the bug is purely in the dW (bwd grad), and specifically the dW GEMM. dX must also be OK (else loss-affecting? no, dX affects earlier-layer grads). Actually layer1 grads are LESS wrong than layer0 → consistent with a dX propagation issue OR a dW issue. Since loss is fine, fwd is fine.\n\nLet me run the dW isolation test (`test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands`) which directly checks the dW GEMM on its own operands — this will tell me if it's the dW GEMM specifically."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"