ens":1058,"cache_read_input_tokens":256676,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1058,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbyJ6hSR5XuWCcxmFYazS","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d46a5061-0688-4dd1-ada3-b915515df084","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:35:14.307Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspace/SuperGrok1.5","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","version":"2.1.173","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"sprightly-pondering-dewdrop"}
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/subagents/agent-aecd237c42ad37eea.jsonl:556:{"parentUuid":"b365f50a-20f9-4b8c-b0c0-e58812237ef2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aecd237c42ad37eea","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_017Mgjt7BfDxLXGZ6rKmiJPt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018UuVa3vHx5hdbBs1FkSLye","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/SuperGrok1.5\ngit add csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh tuning/mamba_bench.py\ngit commit -F - <<'EOF'\nmamba TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) from the decoder twin — -4.9% @ d=128\n\nThe Mamba L3-TC GEMM engine (mbtc::tc_gemm_block_unpipelined) was a DUPLICATE of the\ndecoder's (not a shared helper), so the decoder's H1/H3 wins (627d134, a12c376) were\nNOT live for Mamba — BUT unlike the ViT twin the Mamba engine had kept the decoder's\nexact structure (S-stage ring + stage_k/issue_k lambdas + acc[MaxAtomsM]), so this is\na near-verbatim port (dectc→mbtc, kDec→kMb renames). Production TILE_M=128 (the wgmma.cuh\nsubstrate default, included before the Mamba header's #ifndef) → kAtomsM=2, so Mamba\nfwd/dX DO use the 2-wide interleave (not a no-op), and dW raises MaxAtomsM 1→2.\n\nH1 (engine): m64 atoms processed in GROUPS of kIL=min(MaxAtomsM,SG_TUNED_MB_GEMM_\nINTERLEAVE=2). Each k-step stages the kIL A-tiles (slot s, atom ai at\nsmemA+(s·kMbAtomsPerSlot+ai)·kMbTcSmemA1) + ONE shared B-tile, issues the kIL wgmmas\nback-to-back into INDEPENDENT fragments acc[kIL], single per-k wait (the S=2 double-\nbuffer overlaps stage(k+1) with the group's MMAs). Two wins: tensor-pipe overlap of the\nindependent atoms + B staged once per group. Ascending-k preserved → bit-identical\nnumerics + A/A/A. MbTcSmem.sA grows to kMbTcStages·kMbAtomsPerSlot(=2) A-tiles.\n\nH3 (dW driver): a dW work item owns a GROUP of up to kMbDwIL(=kMbMaxIL=2) consecutive\natoms. Touched mb_dw_groups/atoms, mbtc_dw_total_tiles, mbtc_dw_decode (→m_group),\nmbtc_dw_run_tile + _splitk (MaxAtomsM=kMbDwIL, g_atoms), kMbDwTileFloats (kMbDwIL·64·N),\nkMbDwTilesPerLayer (kMbDwMGroups), the split-K reduce (group rows). Mamba dW atom counts:\nin_proj(512→8, even), x_proj(dbc=40→1, ODD), dt_proj(256→4), out_proj(128→2). The ODD\nx_proj is the one weight the decoder's all-even shortcut would have broken — handled by\nthe ragged-tail logic (g_atoms=min, engine breaks after 1 atom, reduce reads only valid\nrows); its split-K scratch grows by one 64×N slot/N-tile/chunk (x_proj's group reserves\n2 atoms, 1 valid) — accepted, documented in-source.\n\nREGISTER BUDGET (the task's mamba caveat — 255 regs / occ-1 zero margin): the interleave\nheld the line. ptxas (fused_mamba_megakernel_tc, OptId 0): 255 regs UNCHANGED, spill\nstores 40B UNCHANGED (loads 108→96B), stack 1424→2224B, smem 14800→18896B (≪ 48KB).\nOccupancy-1 preserved (the GridBarrier launcher did NOT refuse) and — critically — the\nregister-pressure-sensitive prodigy/mamba + supergrok2/mamba cells still pass A/A/A\n(see gates). kIL stayed 2; no fallback needed.\n\nMEASURED (single H100, tuning/mamba_bench.py, production B=16384, median of 5):\n  HEAD baseline:        108.03 ms/step (9.26 steps/s)\n  H1+H3 (interleave=2): 102.70 ms/step (9.74 steps/s)  −4.9%\n  serial refactor (interleave=1): 105.65 ms — the interleave itself is −2.8%.\n\nGATES:\n  * wiring_check --require-all: 33/33 (mamba 11/11 L3-TC) after _ops rebuild.\n  * tail-gate adamw/mamba (Δp 4.8e-7, m 2.3e-7/v 9.1e-7, A/A/A loss+grad+param\n    bit-identical) + prodigy/mamba (Δp 1.8e-12, state 0/0, A/A/A bit-identical):\n    PASS, after production _ops rebuild — the PRODUCTION L3-TC A/A/A determinism holds.\n  * decoder TC 18/18 + vit TC 21/21 unaffected.\n\nPRE-EXISTING (NOT a regression — verified by checking out HEAD's headers + rerunning):\n  test_mamba_tc.py is 3-fail / 2-pass at HEAD 276861d ALREADY: test_tc_single_step_grad_\n  parity, test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands, test_tc_determinism FAIL on the\n  unmodified baseline (the JIT-TU's out_proj-L1 dW is in the bf16 noise floor — ref.max\n  ~5.6e-4 — so rel~1.0; and the JIT-TU A/A/A grad race is the known mamba register-\n  pressure condition the __noinline__ mbtc_backward_tile mitigates but does not fully\n  close at B=64). My port produces the IDENTICAL 3-fail/2-pass set — it neither fixes nor\n  worsens these. The shipped path (production _ops L3-TC) A/A/A IS green (tail-gates\n  above). HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md already marks the L3 megacells 🟡 numeric-unvalidated.\n\ntuning/mamba_bench.py: new coexisting-variant bench (no decoder-only bench for Mamba)\nwith a -D SG_TUNED_MB_GEMM_INTERLEAVE knob.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\necho \"=== commit done ===\"; git log --oneline -3","description":"Commit the mamba TC port"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2436,"cache_read_input_tokens":318190,"output_tokens":2663,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2436},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2663,"cache_read_input_tokens":318190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2436,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbyK3NCpC9YRq7qMeGNVC","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a029f1ec-9e35-42bf-acc7-57d51a3397c1","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:48:00.049Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspace/SuperGrok1.5","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","version":"2.1.173","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"sprightly-pondering-dewdrop"}
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/subagents/agent-aecd237c42ad37eea.jsonl:567:{"parentUuid":"fc169170-5845-4527-bccc-c9bcdc384e78","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aecd237c42ad37eea","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01R9RDzgaTsqi3ZzhxZmpxSk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both commits are complete and clean. The task is fully done. Let me write the final deliverable report.\n\n---\n\n## Task #24 Phase 1 — COMPLETE\n\nBoth decoder hill-climb wins (H1 forward/dX GEMM interleave + H3 dW tile interleave) ported to the **vit** and **mamba** megakernel twins. Both landed green and committed.\n\n### Shared-vs-duplicated (the first thing the task asked to measure, not assume)\nThe GEMM engine is **DUPLICATED, not shared** — neither twin inherited H1. Each model has its own `tc_gemm_block_unpipelined` in its own namespace (`vittc::`, `mbtc::`), and neither references `dectc::`. So H1 was **not** already live for either; both the engine (H1) and the dW driver (H3) had to be ported per-model. Critically, the two twins had **diverged differently** from the decoder:\n- **mamba** kept the decoder's exact structure (S-stage ring + `stage_k`/`issue_k` lambdas + `acc[MaxAtomsM]`) → near-verbatim port (`dectc`→`mbtc` renames).\n- **vit** had been rewritten to a **single reused accumulator with no ring** — because vit's `kAtomsM=17` made `acc[17]` spill to local memory (C7515). So vit was a port to a structurally *different* (unpipelined) engine, not a copy.\n\n### Per-model before/after (single H100, production B=16384, median of 5; new `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py` mirroring `decoder_bench.py`)\n| Model | HEAD baseline | H1+H3 | Δ | serial-refactor (interleave=1) A/B |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **vit** | 166.59 ms | **123.58 ms** | **−25.8%** | 146.43 ms (interleave itself −15.6%) |\n| **mamba** | 108.03 ms | **102.70 ms** | **−4.9%** | 105.65 ms (interleave itself −2.8%) |\n\nvit far exceeded the expected \"modest\" gain because the interleave **eliminated the engine's register spills** (see below) on top of the MMA-overlap/operand-sharing win. (mamba's TILE_M=128→kAtomsM=2, so its fwd/dX *do* interleave — not the no-op I first suspected before checking.)\n\n### ptxas reg/spill deltas (`fused_*_megakernel_tc`, OptId 0 = AdamW)\n| | vit baseline | vit after | mamba baseline | mamba after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Registers | 255 | 255 | 255 | **255 (held)** |\n| Spill stores | **6452 B** | **0 B** | 40 B | 40 B |\n| Spill loads | 6676 B | 0 B | 108 B | 96 B |\n| Stack | 2704 B | 672 B | 1424 B | 2224 B |\n| smem | 7664 B | 9712 B | 14800 B | 18896 B |\n\n**Mamba's 255-reg/occ-1 zero-margin caveat held** — kIL=2, occupancy-1 preserved (the GridBarrier launcher did not refuse), spills unchanged, **no fallback to kIL=1 needed**. The register-pressure-sensitive prodigy/mamba and supergrok2/mamba cells still pass A/A/A. Even-atom assumption: verified per-weight; mamba's **x_proj (Nout=40 → 1 atom, ODD)** is handled by the ragged-tail logic (the one weight the decoder's all-even shortcut would have broken) — it cost one extra 64×N split-K slot, documented in-source. vit weights are all even.\n\n### Gate outputs (raw, all after production `_ops` rebuild)\n- **wiring_check --require-all: 33/33** (decoder 11/11, vit 11/11, mamba 11/11, all `L3-TC-megakernel(wgmma)`).\n- **Tail-gates (the L3-TC cell parity + A/A/A, with the REAL optimizers):**\n  - `adamw/vit` → PASS: Δp 2.4e-7, m 2.0e-7/v 9.5e-7; **A/A/A loss+grad+param bit-identical**.\n  - `supergrok2/vit` → PASS: **A/A/A loss+grad+param+sharp+gru all bit-identical**, B1 parity 5e-7.\n  - `adamw/mamba` → PASS: Δp 4.8e-7, m 2.3e-7/v 9.1e-7; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n  - `prodigy/mamba` → PASS: Δp 1.8e-12, state 0/0; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n- **TC unit suites:** `test_vit_tc.py` **21/21** (incl. Nout=384→6-atom & 512→8-atom multi-group dW, dW stride gate, full-cell parity, determinism). `test_decoder_tc.py` **18/18** (unaffected — confirms the shared-dispatcher recompile is clean).\n\n### What I kept / reverted, and why\n**Nothing reverted.** Both ports kept.\n\nThe one honest caveat: **`test_mamba_tc.py` is 3-fail/2-pass — but PRE-EXISTING at HEAD, not a regression.** I verified by checking out HEAD's mamba headers, rebuilding, and rerunning: `test_tc_single_step_grad_parity`, `test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands`, and `test_tc_determinism` **already fail on unmodified 276861d**. Cause: the JIT-TU's out_proj-L1 dW is in the bf16 noise floor (ref.max ~5.6e-4 → rel~1.0), and the JIT-TU A/A/A grad race at B=64 is the known mamba register-pressure condition that `__noinline__ mbtc_backward_tile` mitigates but doesn't fully close. **My port reproduces the identical 3-fail/2-pass set** — neither fixes nor worsens it. The *shipped* path (production `_ops` L3-TC) A/A/A **is** green (the mamba tail-gates above prove it). This matches HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md already marking the L3 megacells 🟡 numeric-unvalidated.\n\n### Commits\n- `5273f99` — vit TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −25.8% @ d=128\n- `f560b89` — mamba TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −4.9% @ d=128\n\nBoth touch only their model's `model_stage_*_tc.cuh` + `fused_*_megakernel.cuh` smem struct (+ vit's selftest TU `mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`), gated behind new `SG_TUNED_{VIT,MB}_GEMM_INTERLEAVE` knobs (default 2; =1 restores the old serial path bit-for-bit). New bench harnesses `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py`. Files (all absolute):\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_vit_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_vit_megakernel.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/vit_bench.py`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/mamba_bench.py`\n\nThe big payoff lands at the ladder dims later (as the task anticipated); at production d the structural ports are in, green, and — for vit — already a large win from the spill elimination."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_read_input_tokens":325326,"output_tokens":2763,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":792},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2763,"cache_read_input_tokens":325326,"cache_creation_input_tokens":792,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":792,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CbyKBnCB48PaWxDgQaKhY","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4cb254cd-0268-498d-b89d-6b6703421108","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:49:54.717Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspace/SuperGrok1.5","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","version":"2.1.173","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"sprightly-pondering-dewdrop"}
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338.jsonl:3611:{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:49:54.825Z","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aecd237c42ad37eea</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01VzVdwUhq2rg5eJp4HThyd5</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-0/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/tasks/aecd237c42ad37eea.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Propagate interleave wins to vit/mamba\" completed</summary>\n<result>Both commits are complete and clean. The task is fully done. Let me write the final deliverable report.\n\n---\n\n## Task #24 Phase 1 — COMPLETE\n\nBoth decoder hill-climb wins (H1 forward/dX GEMM interleave + H3 dW tile interleave) ported to the **vit** and **mamba** megakernel twins. Both landed green and committed.\n\n### Shared-vs-duplicated (the first thing the task asked to measure, not assume)\nThe GEMM engine is **DUPLICATED, not shared** — neither twin inherited H1. Each model has its own `tc_gemm_block_unpipelined` in its own namespace (`vittc::`, `mbtc::`), and neither references `dectc::`. So H1 was **not** already live for either; both the engine (H1) and the dW driver (H3) had to be ported per-model. Critically, the two twins had **diverged differently** from the decoder:\n- **mamba** kept the decoder's exact structure (S-stage ring + `stage_k`/`issue_k` lambdas + `acc[MaxAtomsM]`) → near-verbatim port (`dectc`→`mbtc` renames).\n- **vit** had been rewritten to a **single reused accumulator with no ring** — because vit's `kAtomsM=17` made `acc[17]` spill to local memory (C7515). So vit was a port to a structurally *different* (unpipelined) engine, not a copy.\n\n### Per-model before/after (single H100, production B=16384, median of 5; new `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py` mirroring `decoder_bench.py`)\n| Model | HEAD baseline | H1+H3 | Δ | serial-refactor (interleave=1) A/B |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **vit** | 166.59 ms | **123.58 ms** | **−25.8%** | 146.43 ms (interleave itself −15.6%) |\n| **mamba** | 108.03 ms | **102.70 ms** | **−4.9%** | 105.65 ms (interleave itself −2.8%) |\n\nvit far exceeded the expected \"modest\" gain because the interleave **eliminated the engine's register spills** (see below) on top of the MMA-overlap/operand-sharing win. (mamba's TILE_M=128→kAtomsM=2, so its fwd/dX *do* interleave — not the no-op I first suspected before checking.)\n\n### ptxas reg/spill deltas (`fused_*_megakernel_tc`, OptId 0 = AdamW)\n| | vit baseline | vit after | mamba baseline | mamba after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Registers | 255 | 255 | 255 | **255 (held)** |\n| Spill stores | **6452 B** | **0 B** | 40 B | 40 B |\n| Spill loads | 6676 B | 0 B | 108 B | 96 B |\n| Stack | 2704 B | 672 B | 1424 B | 2224 B |\n| smem | 7664 B | 9712 B | 14800 B | 18896 B |\n\n**Mamba's 255-reg/occ-1 zero-margin caveat held** — kIL=2, occupancy-1 preserved (the GridBarrier launcher did not refuse), spills unchanged, **no fallback to kIL=1 needed**. The register-pressure-sensitive prodigy/mamba and supergrok2/mamba cells still pass A/A/A. Even-atom assumption: verified per-weight; mamba's **x_proj (Nout=40 → 1 atom, ODD)** is handled by the ragged-tail logic (the one weight the decoder's all-even shortcut would have broken) — it cost one extra 64×N split-K slot, documented in-source. vit weights are all even.\n\n### Gate outputs (raw, all after production `_ops` rebuild)\n- **wiring_check --require-all: 33/33** (decoder 11/11, vit 11/11, mamba 11/11, all `L3-TC-megakernel(wgmma)`).\n- **Tail-gates (the L3-TC cell parity + A/A/A, with the REAL optimizers):**\n  - `adamw/vit` → PASS: Δp 2.4e-7, m 2.0e-7/v 9.5e-7; **A/A/A loss+grad+param bit-identical**.\n  - `supergrok2/vit` → PASS: **A/A/A loss+grad+param+sharp+gru all bit-identical**, B1 parity 5e-7.\n  - `adamw/mamba` → PASS: Δp 4.8e-7, m 2.3e-7/v 9.1e-7; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n  - `prodigy/mamba` → PASS: Δp 1.8e-12, state 0/0; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n- **TC unit suites:** `test_vit_tc.py` **21/21** (incl. Nout=384→6-atom &amp; 512→8-atom multi-group dW, dW stride gate, full-cell parity, determinism). `test_decoder_tc.py` **18/18** (unaffected — confirms the shared-dispatcher recompile is clean).\n\n### What I kept / reverted, and why\n**Nothing reverted.** Both ports kept.\n\nThe one honest caveat: **`test_mamba_tc.py` is 3-fail/2-pass — but PRE-EXISTING at HEAD, not a regression.** I verified by checking out HEAD's mamba headers, rebuilding, and rerunning: `test_tc_single_step_grad_parity`, `test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands`, and `test_tc_determinism` **already fail on unmodified 276861d**. Cause: the JIT-TU's out_proj-L1 dW is in the bf16 noise floor (ref.max ~5.6e-4 → rel~1.0), and the JIT-TU A/A/A grad race at B=64 is the known mamba register-pressure condition that `__noinline__ mbtc_backward_tile` mitigates but doesn't fully close. **My port reproduces the identical 3-fail/2-pass set** — neither fixes nor worsens it. The *shipped* path (production `_ops` L3-TC) A/A/A **is** green (the mamba tail-gates above prove it). This matches HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md already marking the L3 megacells 🟡 numeric-unvalidated.\n\n### Commits\n- `5273f99` — vit TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −25.8% @ d=128\n- `f560b89` — mamba TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −4.9% @ d=128\n\nBoth touch only their model's `model_stage_*_tc.cuh` + `fused_*_megakernel.cuh` smem struct (+ vit's selftest TU `mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`), gated behind new `SG_TUNED_{VIT,MB}_GEMM_INTERLEAVE` knobs (default 2; =1 restores the old serial path bit-for-bit). New bench harnesses `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py`. Files (all absolute):\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_vit_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_vit_megakernel.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/vit_bench.py`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/mamba_bench.py`\n\nThe big payoff lands at the ladder dims later (as the task anticipated); at production d the structural ports are in, green, and — for vit — already a large win from the spill elimination.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>327576</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>194</tool_uses><duration_ms>3730391</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/claude_session_archive/projects/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338.jsonl:3613:{"parentUuid":"10709b71-68ca-4328-87e4-ab098f2ea49d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"217b6462-38d1-4b05-a809-f5bad0e6eaaf","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aecd237c42ad37eea</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01VzVdwUhq2rg5eJp4HThyd5</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-0/-/80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338/tasks/aecd237c42ad37eea.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Propagate interleave wins to vit/mamba\" completed</summary>\n<result>Both commits are complete and clean. The task is fully done. Let me write the final deliverable report.\n\n---\n\n## Task #24 Phase 1 — COMPLETE\n\nBoth decoder hill-climb wins (H1 forward/dX GEMM interleave + H3 dW tile interleave) ported to the **vit** and **mamba** megakernel twins. Both landed green and committed.\n\n### Shared-vs-duplicated (the first thing the task asked to measure, not assume)\nThe GEMM engine is **DUPLICATED, not shared** — neither twin inherited H1. Each model has its own `tc_gemm_block_unpipelined` in its own namespace (`vittc::`, `mbtc::`), and neither references `dectc::`. So H1 was **not** already live for either; both the engine (H1) and the dW driver (H3) had to be ported per-model. Critically, the two twins had **diverged differently** from the decoder:\n- **mamba** kept the decoder's exact structure (S-stage ring + `stage_k`/`issue_k` lambdas + `acc[MaxAtomsM]`) → near-verbatim port (`dectc`→`mbtc` renames).\n- **vit** had been rewritten to a **single reused accumulator with no ring** — because vit's `kAtomsM=17` made `acc[17]` spill to local memory (C7515). So vit was a port to a structurally *different* (unpipelined) engine, not a copy.\n\n### Per-model before/after (single H100, production B=16384, median of 5; new `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py` mirroring `decoder_bench.py`)\n| Model | HEAD baseline | H1+H3 | Δ | serial-refactor (interleave=1) A/B |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **vit** | 166.59 ms | **123.58 ms** | **−25.8%** | 146.43 ms (interleave itself −15.6%) |\n| **mamba** | 108.03 ms | **102.70 ms** | **−4.9%** | 105.65 ms (interleave itself −2.8%) |\n\nvit far exceeded the expected \"modest\" gain because the interleave **eliminated the engine's register spills** (see below) on top of the MMA-overlap/operand-sharing win. (mamba's TILE_M=128→kAtomsM=2, so its fwd/dX *do* interleave — not the no-op I first suspected before checking.)\n\n### ptxas reg/spill deltas (`fused_*_megakernel_tc`, OptId 0 = AdamW)\n| | vit baseline | vit after | mamba baseline | mamba after |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Registers | 255 | 255 | 255 | **255 (held)** |\n| Spill stores | **6452 B** | **0 B** | 40 B | 40 B |\n| Spill loads | 6676 B | 0 B | 108 B | 96 B |\n| Stack | 2704 B | 672 B | 1424 B | 2224 B |\n| smem | 7664 B | 9712 B | 14800 B | 18896 B |\n\n**Mamba's 255-reg/occ-1 zero-margin caveat held** — kIL=2, occupancy-1 preserved (the GridBarrier launcher did not refuse), spills unchanged, **no fallback to kIL=1 needed**. The register-pressure-sensitive prodigy/mamba and supergrok2/mamba cells still pass A/A/A. Even-atom assumption: verified per-weight; mamba's **x_proj (Nout=40 → 1 atom, ODD)** is handled by the ragged-tail logic (the one weight the decoder's all-even shortcut would have broken) — it cost one extra 64×N split-K slot, documented in-source. vit weights are all even.\n\n### Gate outputs (raw, all after production `_ops` rebuild)\n- **wiring_check --require-all: 33/33** (decoder 11/11, vit 11/11, mamba 11/11, all `L3-TC-megakernel(wgmma)`).\n- **Tail-gates (the L3-TC cell parity + A/A/A, with the REAL optimizers):**\n  - `adamw/vit` → PASS: Δp 2.4e-7, m 2.0e-7/v 9.5e-7; **A/A/A loss+grad+param bit-identical**.\n  - `supergrok2/vit` → PASS: **A/A/A loss+grad+param+sharp+gru all bit-identical**, B1 parity 5e-7.\n  - `adamw/mamba` → PASS: Δp 4.8e-7, m 2.3e-7/v 9.1e-7; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n  - `prodigy/mamba` → PASS: Δp 1.8e-12, state 0/0; **A/A/A bit-identical**.\n- **TC unit suites:** `test_vit_tc.py` **21/21** (incl. Nout=384→6-atom &amp; 512→8-atom multi-group dW, dW stride gate, full-cell parity, determinism). `test_decoder_tc.py` **18/18** (unaffected — confirms the shared-dispatcher recompile is clean).\n\n### What I kept / reverted, and why\n**Nothing reverted.** Both ports kept.\n\nThe one honest caveat: **`test_mamba_tc.py` is 3-fail/2-pass — but PRE-EXISTING at HEAD, not a regression.** I verified by checking out HEAD's mamba headers, rebuilding, and rerunning: `test_tc_single_step_grad_parity`, `test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands`, and `test_tc_determinism` **already fail on unmodified 276861d**. Cause: the JIT-TU's out_proj-L1 dW is in the bf16 noise floor (ref.max ~5.6e-4 → rel~1.0), and the JIT-TU A/A/A grad race at B=64 is the known mamba register-pressure condition that `__noinline__ mbtc_backward_tile` mitigates but doesn't fully close. **My port reproduces the identical 3-fail/2-pass set** — neither fixes nor worsens it. The *shipped* path (production `_ops` L3-TC) A/A/A **is** green (the mamba tail-gates above prove it). This matches HARDWARE_VALIDATION.md already marking the L3 megacells 🟡 numeric-unvalidated.\n\n### Commits\n- `5273f99` — vit TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −25.8% @ d=128\n- `f560b89` — mamba TC: port M-atom interleave (H1+H3) — −4.9% @ d=128\n\nBoth touch only their model's `model_stage_*_tc.cuh` + `fused_*_megakernel.cuh` smem struct (+ vit's selftest TU `mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`), gated behind new `SG_TUNED_{VIT,MB}_GEMM_INTERLEAVE` knobs (default 2; =1 restores the old serial path bit-for-bit). New bench harnesses `tuning/{vit,mamba}_bench.py`. Files (all absolute):\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_vit_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_vit_megakernel.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/mega_vit_real_adamw_tc.cu`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/csrc/fused/sm_90/fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh`\n- `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/vit_bench.py`, `/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/tuning/mamba_bench.py`\n\nThe big payoff lands at the ladder dims later (as the task anticipated); at production d the structural ports are in, green, and — for vit — already a large win from the spill elimination.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>327576</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>194</tool_uses><duration_ms>3730391</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"20ec21b8-c3ef-4fd1-9a30-6334a032eddc","timestamp":"2026-06-12T11:49:54.867Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/workspace/SuperGrok1.5","sessionId":"80b51e31-b580-43b6-8244-fd7633ee1338","version":"2.1.173","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"sprightly-pondering-dewdrop"}
