/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.perf/author_queue3_report.json:22:        "fix": "Authored the M0 mamba body-rewire (the GPU-iteration-gated integration of the dormant scaffold) under #if SG_TUNED_MB_PROJ_WGMMA, split cleanly into two independently-gated sub-levers, in my isolated worktree only.\n\nFWD-GEMM HALF (transport-only by construction, gate-green-by-precedent, CPU-provable non-perturbing):\n- C1 in P0: mb_proj_wbf_convert fills the bf16 projection-weight cache (fenced by B0).\n- New mbtc_materialize_sample_x (in model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh) called in P1 after each sample's mb_forward_sample (before mb_backward_sample reuses smem / before the next sample overwrites it): materializes the 5 converted projections' INPUTS X (in/out/gate/up/down) to the MbActs HBM region at rows [b*kSeq, b*kSeq+kSeq). xn and h1n (not retained by the scalar fwd) are recomputed with the IDENTICAL fp32 RMSNorm the oracle ran (same multiply association); y_gated and prod from retained LayerAct. Every stored value is __float2bfloat16 of the exact oracle fp32 -> bf16-rounded reference, element-owned, no reduction/atomics. The scan + scalar fwd/bwd are byte-for-byte untouched, and nothing consumes these acts until the dW half goes LIVE, so turning the fwd half ON changes grads NOT AT ALL (only adds plumbing) -- verifiably transport-only.\n\ndW HALF (needs-parity-fp32-reassoc, S1-class, GPU-only-revalidatable) -- structured + compiled but the parity-bearing step reported as TODO:\n- A P2-dW output-stationary phase (mbtc_proj_dw_run_tile, gt % nCTA ownership, full-T K-contraction, ascending-t, no atomics) that overwrites the 5 weights' reduced grad with the reassociated wgmma dW. Gated under SG_TUNED_MB_PROJ_WGMMA_DW (defaults to the master; set =0 to land the fwd half alone -- the decoder fold-A-reverts-alone discipline).\n- The dY-adjoint capture (dY_in=[dx_main|dz], dY_outp, dY_gate, dY_up, dY_down) is TRANSIENT in the scalar bwd, so capturing it needs hooks inside mb_backward_sample/mb_mixer_bwd/mb_swiglu_bwd. That is the parity-changing, GPU-only step and is LEFT AS THE EXPLICIT TODO. The actual grad overwrite is double-guarded by SG_TUNED_MB_PROJ_WGMMA_DW_LIVE (default OFF) so the GEMM machinery compiles/reviews without risking zeroed grads before dY is wired.\n\nWORKTREE NOTE: the worktree was created from a stale base (7cf02af) that lacked the target files (fused_mamba_megakernel.cuh / model_stage_mamba_tc.cuh). I reset my OWN worktree branch to the main-tree HEAD 3bf77a8 (decoder PIPE=1/S4 + SG11 + ViT-B1 committed) -- this moves only my isolated worktree branch pointer; the main tree (branch claude/h100-audit-maximal) and its working copy were never touched. Applied .perf/M0_mamba_integration_scaffold.patch first (the superset scaffold; M0_mamba_wgmma_projections.patch is a strict subset already contained in it), then authored the rewire on top.",
/workspace/SuperGrok1.5/.perf/author_queue3_report.json:30:        "verified_cpu": "YES (CPU-only, no GPU). (1) BYTE-IDENTICAL OFF: nvcc -ptx of the mamba-TC AdamW megakernel (torch-included harness, sm_90a) sha256=482854bcfccf73b6b24e29703a80edde497791555d4dcfe675e55ff18f978e09 -- IDENTICAL pre-rewire (scaffold-only) vs post-rewire, same compile path. (2) nvcc -c exit 0 for all ON configs: master =1 (152 regs, 0 spill, 368B smem); master + DW=0 fwd-half-alone; master + DW_LIVE=1 full dW GEMM (214 regs, 0 spill -- under the 255 cap so occ=1 holds, the SG_MBTC_MIN_BLOCKS_PER_SM=1 design point); master + PROFILE=1 (slot 4 = p2-dwgemm). (3) ws-agreement proof (host mb_tc_workspace_floats vs kernel carve_end) re-run with my edits: slack 0 OFF, slack 0 ON, slack 1-2 ON+PROFILE (the documented fixed pad) at all (T,nCTA) in {1,16,132}x{64,1024,8192} -- no under-allocation, the single-source mb_proj_wgmma_floats(T) term cannot drift (ViT-IMA invariant preserved; I did not touch the carve). (4) pytest --collect-only tests/hw/test_mamba_tc.py -> 5 tests collected (harness intact, incl. test_tc_proj_dw_exact_on_own_operands). (5) The rewire-only diff git apply --check exit 0 onto a fresh scaffold-applied tree and reproduces my worktree files byte-for-byte.",
